; The console reads once the configuration's task pauses, so a form from
; standard input runs while a later form of the configuration is paused.
configuration paused
> (begin (display "from standard input") (newline) (sleep-for 0.3))
from standard input
configuration resumed
; Values, a pause and an error.
> (define x 5)
> (values x "five")
5
"five"
> (begin (sleep-for 0.1) 'slept)
slept
> (error 'check "bad value" 7)
! check: bad value with irritant 7
; A line may hold several forms, and the console reads the next once the
; form before has ended, pauses included.
> (begin (sleep-for 0.1) 'first) 'second
first
second
; Each form is evaluated as the REPL.
> (current-owner)
(repl)
; Forms are read back as the same data, whatever the printer's settings.
> (print-length 2)
> (length (list 1 2 3 4 5))
5
> (print-length #f)
> (gensym? '#{g1 console-test})
#t
> (let ([v '#0=(a . #0#)]) (eq? v (cdr v)))
#t
; Reloading the console keeps its place in standard input.
> (eval-file console-file) 'after-reload
after-reload
> 'next
next
; Unloading it stops reading: Tuna runs on until something ends it.
> (run-with-timer 0.2 (lambda () (display "still running") (exit)))
#<timer>
> (unload-module! '(console))
still running
> (display "never read")
